\section{Ablations and Sensitivity}
We evaluate Max-Rate ($\beta{=}0$) and No-Coverage ($\gamma{=}0$) variants under hotspot traffic (Table~\ref{tab:ablation}). Max-Rate slightly increases sum-rate but reduces energy efficiency; No-Coverage harms cell-edge users. The full model best balances objectives. We also varied $(\alpha,\beta,\gamma)$ and observed smooth trade-offs: higher $\beta$ reduces $M_b$ usage and power; higher $\gamma$ increases protective downtilts. Penalty $\Lambda$ across $[5,20]$ yields identical decoded solutions, indicating robust feasibility enforcement.

